# Designer workflow in Cursor

This plugin is for **designers**. The primary flow is **design request → research → HTML prototype → iterate**. Default to research summaries and canvas HTML artifacts, not deep engineering codegen.

## Primary workflow

| Step | Command / agent | Output |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1. Research | `/design-research` or **Design Request** agent | Inspiration & pattern summary |
| 2. Prototype | `/design-prototype` | Mobile HTML canvas artifact |
| 3. Iterate | `/design-iterate` | Updated artifact + changelog |

Run all three with checkpoints: `/design-request <brief>`

## Secondary capabilities (Figma / FigJam)

| Designer intent | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Existing team frame specs | `/inspect-design` or `figma-inspect-handoff` skill |
| Workshop board summary | `/figjam-summary` |
| Light mobile codegen (explicit ask) | `figma-design-to-code` skill — single screen only |
| Code Connect (future) | `figma-code-connect` skill (stub) |

Use Figma/FigJam during **research** when URLs are available — not as a substitute for HTML prototypes.

## Default behavior

1. **Research before prototype** — Gather inspiration and scope unless user skips research.
2. **HTML before Figma polish** — Canvas artifact is the review vehicle for MVP.
3. **One screen at a time** — Prototype focused flows; expand when asked.
4. **Version iterations** — Every feedback round updates changelog and version comment.
5. **Preserve design intent** — Call out ambiguities instead of guessing product decisions.

## Review checklist (before Figma polish)

- [ ] Prototype matches brief and research scope
- [ ] 390px mobile viewport and safe areas verified
- [ ] Interactive states documented (default, error, empty as scoped)
- [ ] Touch targets ≥ 44px; focus states visible
- [ ] Changelog and open questions up to date in companion notes
- [ ] Platform-specific variants noted if applicable

## What not to do in MVP

- Do not sync or export design tokens (no token path configured).
- Do not scaffold full apps, navigation stacks, or CI pipelines unless explicitly requested.
- Do not replace Figma for final polish — HTML prototype precedes Figma refinement.
- Do not default to Figma-handoff-only when a design **request** is submitted.

## Example prompts (designer-friendly)

- `/design-request Mobile savings nudge at checkout — bottom sheet, trust copy, 390px`
- `/design-research Sticky CTA patterns above home indicator on iOS`
- `/design-prototype Login screen from research — email, SSO, error state`
- `/design-iterate prototypes/login-v1.html — shorten headline, add forgot password link`
- "Inspect our existing login frame for reference: [Figma URL]" (secondary)
